      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1365247224,
      "text": "Annona mucosa is a species of flowering plant in the custard-apple family, Annonaceae, that is native to tropical South America. It is cultivated for its edible fruits, commonly known as biribá, lemon meringue pie fruit, wild sugar-apple, or rollinia throughout the world's tropics and subtropics."
